  "description": "ROSNEU crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H64 Dy6 Mo4 N4 O40 2-,2(H4 N1 1+),4(C1 H4 O1),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mo1 (Mo) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Mo1A (Mo) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1F (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2F (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mo1F (Mo) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1G (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Mo1G (Mo) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.342-4.307 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 83.77-165.99°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (NH4)2[Dy6Mo4O12(rac-L)4(OOCCH3)8]·4CH3OH·6H2O.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
